description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, remove a duplicated block that was landed twice by a previous apply.

Inside the enclosing `if (dist > ANCHOR_REGION_SLACK_LINES) {` block there are currently TWO identical `if (regionHint) { ... } else { ... }` statements, one immediately after the other. Exactly one of them must remain.

ANCHOR. This exact text currently occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file — the closing brace of the first copy followed immediately by the opening of the second copy:

            }
            if (regionHint) {
              anchorFarFromRegion = true;

Replace that three-line sequence with just its first line:

            }

That deletes the second, redundant `if (regionHint) { ... } else { ... }` statement while leaving the first one and the enclosing `if (dist > ...)` block intact.

AFTER THE CHANGE, the enclosing block must read exactly:

          if (dist > ANCHOR_REGION_SLACK_LINES) {
            if (regionHint) {
              anchorFarFromRegion = true;
              console.warn(`[fc-anchor-region] planned anchor for ${op.path} is unique but ${dist} lines from the EXPLICIT region (line ${center + 1}) — re-deriving from the offered anchors instead`);
            } else {
              console.warn(`[fc-anchor-region] planned anchor for ${op.path} is unique but ${dist} lines from a region located ONLY from mined identifiers (line ${center + 1}) — TRUSTING THE UNIQUE ANCHOR: a mined region is a guess, a unique literal match is a fact`);
            }
          }

SUCCESS CONDITION: the file contains EXACTLY ONE occurrence of the string `TRUSTING THE UNIQUE ANCHOR` and EXACTLY ONE occurrence of `from the EXPLICIT region`. Both currently occur twice. Verify by counting occurrences, not by reading the diff — a duplicated block typechecks cleanly and reads correctly in a diff, which is precisely why this defect landed.

Change nothing else. Do not touch the top of the file, any import, the enclosing `if (dist > ANCHOR_REGION_SLACK_LINES)` condition, or the surrounding comment. Behaviour must be identical: the first copy already does the right thing, and the second copy is pure redundancy.

